  { q: 'Do ravens use the same nest every year?', a: 'Yes — established raven pairs are highly site-faithful, returning to the same nest or the same cliff face year after year. Nest sites that are used for many years become large, bulky structures as new material is added each season on top of the previous year\'s structure. Some long-occupied raven nests have been recorded over 20+ years of continuous or near-continuous use, reaching substantial dimensions (up to 1.5m deep and 1m wide). The attachment to the nest site is primarily the pair\'s attachment to the territory: the nest is built within the core of their territory, the most valuable location they defend.' },
